# SFDC Agent Swarm (all projects)

The multi-agent framework lives in [Agency-Swarm](https://github.com/lparuchuru-titan/Agency-Swarm) (install via `scripts/install-to-project.sh` or `./install.sh`).

## Before deploy / retrieve / orchestrator / skill refresh

```bash
sfdc-swarm context
# or: python3 ~/.cursor/skills/_shared/show-context.py
```

Use resolved values — never hardcode org aliases:

| Field | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `targetOrgAlias` | Every `sf` command (`--target-org`) |
| `sourcePath` | Package root (`force-app/main/default` or `Master/main/default`) |
| `projectRoot` | Repo root for paths and KB |

Org priority: project `.sf/config.json` → optional `.cursor/sfdc-project/config.json` → `sf config get`.

## Per-project files (optional)

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `.cursor/sfdc-project/config.json` | Jira epic, optional org override |
| `.cursor/swarm/project-topics.json` | Project-specific KB topic stubs |
| `knowledge-base/` | Per-project codebase + connected indexes |
| `.cursor/swarm/.fleet/` | FleetView run state |

Shared across all projects: `~/.cursor/sfdc-knowledge-swarm/knowledge-base/sfdc/` (public Salesforce docs).

This framework does **not** run automatically on every Cursor chat message.

| Trigger | What runs |
|---------|-----------|
| FleetView **Run orchestrator** | Full LangGraph pipeline |
| `sfdc-swarm orchestrate "…"` | Same, from terminal |
| Scheduled skill refresh | KB/index only (usually $0) |
| **Normal Cursor chat** | Your Cursor agent only — unless you ask it to run the swarm |

To use from Cursor chat, say explicitly: *"Run the orchestrator for …"* or *"Use sfdc-swarm orchestrate …"*

## Agency Swarm-style Cursor template

Plain-English CEO delegation (Agency Swarm pattern adapted for Cursor):

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `AGENTS.md` | Agency entry point (read first) |
| `.cursor/agency/agency_manifesto.md` | Shared rules for all agents |
| `.cursor/agency/agency_chart.md` | Who delegates to whom |
| `.cursor/agency/<agent>/instructions.md` | Per-specialist role, goals, workflow |
| `.cursor/rules/agency-swarm-cursor.mdc` | CEO rule — **Apply Intelligently** (rich `description`, no globs) |
| `.cursor/rules/agency-swarm-salesforce-files.mdc` | Auto-attach when editing `force-app/`, `manifest/`, agents |
| `.cursor/agents/ceo.md` | CEO subagent for Task tool |

Regenerate after registry changes: `python3 tools/sfdc-knowledge-swarm/agency_cursor_sync.py`

## Metadata edits (retrieve first)

Before changing any `force-app/` metadata: **retrieve latest from org**, then apply changes on top. See `.cursor/rules/sfdc-metadata-retrieve-first.mdc`.
